{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a stitch task (Task ID: 5411) to implement srd060-date requirements R4.1 through R4.4 for the `cmd/date` utility in the go-unix-utils project. The specific requirements are:\n   - R4.1: Must exit 0 when the date is displayed successfully\n   - R4.2: Must exit 1 when an invalid date string is given or a referenced file does not exist\n   - R4.3: Differential tests must compare stdout and exit codes between Go binary and reference binary via pkg/testutils, using fixed dates via `-d @EPOCH` for deterministic output\n   - R4.4: Tests must cover: default output with fixed epoch, +FORMAT with various conversion specs, -d with epoch and ISO strings, -u UTC mode, -r reference file, padding modifiers, and error cases (invalid date, missing file)\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/date/main.go` (extend with R4 group) and `cmd/date/date_test.go` (add differential tests for R4 group).\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: go vet passes, go build succeeds, R4.1-R4.4 fully implemented, existing tests don't regress, new differential tests pass against gdate.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU reference binary (gdate)\n   - strftime-style format string parsing in Go\n   - Exit code handling (0 for success, 1 for errors)\n   - LC_ALL=C and TZ=UTC for deterministic test output\n   - Fixed epoch timestamps (`-d @EPOCH`) for reproducible tests\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - The cobbler orchestrator manages git; no git commands should be run\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd060-date.yaml`\n     - The SRD defining all requirements for cmd/date