tial tests (R4.3, R4.4) are largely present but the task expects explicit additions/extensions for the R4 group\n   - No code changes have been made yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Large stitch task description with full project context, SRD content, execution constitution, go style constitution, task requirements for implementing srd060-date R4.1-R4.4, files to modify, design decisions, acceptance criteria, and constraints\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — instructing me to provide a summary instead of continuing implementation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Update `cmd/date/main.go` header comment to include R4.1-R4.4\n   - Verify exit code behavior is complete and correct for R4.1 and R4.2\n   - Add additional differential test cases in `cmd/date/date_test.go` covering R4.3 and R4.4 requirements (possibly a dedicated TestDiffExitCodes or similar test function)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/date/...` to verify no errors\n   - Run `go build -o bin/date ./cmd/date/` to verify successful build\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/date/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (srd060-date.yaml, cmd/date/main.go, cmd/date/date_test.go) and was about to plan and implement the R4.1-R4.4 changes. No code modifications have been made yet. The analysis phase was underway — determining what changes are needed:\n   \n   For `cmd/date/main.go`:\n   - Update the package comment from `// Implements srd060-date R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.4.` to `// Implements srd060-date R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.4, R4.1-R4.4.`\n   - The exit code logic (R4.1: exit 0 on success, R4.2: exit 1 on error) is already correctly implemented in the existing `main()` function\n   \n   For `cmd/date/date_test.go`:\n   - Need to add a new test function (e.g., `TestDiffExitCodes`) or extend existing tests to explicitly cover R4.3 and R4.4 requirements\n   - R4.4 specifies test coverage for: default output with fixed epoch, +FORMAT with various conversion specs, -d with epoch and ISO strings, -u UTC mode, -r reference file, padding modifiers, and error cases\n   - Most of these are already covered but need to ensure completeness and possibly add additional edge cases\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue implementing R4.1-R4.4 by:\n   1. Updating the header comment in `cmd/date/main.go` to reference R4.1-R4.4\n   2. Adding any missing differential test cases to `cmd/date/date_test.go` — particularly a dedicated test function for exit code and error behavior testing (R4.3/R4.4)\n   3. Running `go vet`, `go build`, and `go test` to verify acceptance criteria\n   \n   The task description states: \"Implement srd060-date requirement R4.1 as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd060-date requirement R4.2 as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd060-date requirement R4.3 as specified in the SRD\", \"Implement srd060-date requirement R4.4 as specified in the SRD\". Design decisions: \"Extend the existing main.go structure -- do not reorganize or refactor code from prior tasks\" and \"Add new DiffTest entries to the existing tests slice in date_test.go\" and \"Set LC_ALL=C in all new differential test entries\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5411/8340404a-2de1-4d87-aad0-c76d4d4c6cd7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8340404a-2de1-4d87-aad0-c76d4d4c6cd7","uuid":"adad82a5-6401-45c1-9a68-e08355f057f1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T